on-cold-runny-or-blocked-nose-sneezing--gojihvadi-kwatha","name":"Gojihvadi kwatha","nameHi":"गोजिह्वादि क्वाथ","form":"Decoction","howUsed":"internal","caution":"Little safety research exists; avoid in pregnancy and check with a doctor if you take regular medicines. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"common-cold-runny-or-blocked-nose-sneezing--dashamoola-kwatha","name":"Dashamoola kwatha","nameHi":"दशमूल क्वाथ","form":"Decoction","howUsed":"internal","caution":"Little safety research exists; avoid in pregnancy and check with a doctor if you take regular medicines. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"common-cold-runny-or-blocked-nose-sneezing--haridra-khanda","name":"Haridra khanda","nameHi":"हरिद्रा खंड","form":"Granules","howUsed":"internal","caution":"Turmeric may add to the effect of blood thinners; not in pregnancy at medicinal doses. About half sugar by weight; count it if you watch blood sugar. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"common-cold-runny-or-blocked-nose-sneezing--vasavaleha","name":"Vasavaleha","nameHi":"वासावलेह","form":"Herbal jam (avaleha)","howUsed":"internal","caution":"Vasa (adhatoda) is not for use in pregnancy. About half sugar by weight; count it if you watch blood sugar. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"common-cold-runny-or-blocked-nose-sneezing--drakshavaleha","name":"Drakshavaleha","nameHi":"द्राक्षावलेह","form":"Herbal jam (avaleha)","howUsed":"internal","caution":"About half sugar by weight; count it if you watch blood sugar. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"common-cold-runny-or-blocked-nose-sneezing--chitraka-haritaki-avaleha","name":"Chitraka haritaki avaleha","nameHi":"चित्रक हरीतकी अवलेह","form":"Herbal jam (avaleha)","howUsed":"internal","caution":"About half sugar by weight; count it if you watch blood sugar. Laxative. Not for long-term use, children or pregnancy without a doctor's advice. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"common-cold-runny-or-blocked-nose-sneezing--anu-taila","name":"Anu taila","nameHi":"अणु तैल","form":"Oil","howUsed":"nasal drops","caution":"Nasal drops: use only as advised, not for young children, and not during a nosebleed or sinus infection with fever. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."}]},{"id":"occasional-tension-type-headache","title":"Occasional tension-type headache","titleHi":"कभी-कभी तनाव वाला सिरदर्द","otcMedicinesUsuallyUsed":"Paracetamol, ibuprofen, aspirin","seeADoctorIf":"sudden severe headache, headache with fever and stiff neck, weakness, vision change, or after a head injury","source":"Ministry of AYUSH, Ayurvedic Standard Treatment Guidelines (2017), Shiroroga, Table 38.2. https://main.ayush.gov.in/ayurvedic-standard-treatment-guidelines/","options":[{"id":"occasional-tension-type-headache--pathyadi-kwatha","name":"Pathyadi kwatha","nameHi":"पथ्यादि क्वाथ","form":"Decoction","howUsed":"internal","caution":"Laxative. Not for long-term use, children or pregnancy without a doctor's advice. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"occasional-tension-type-headache--cow-s-ghee-nasal-drops-gau-ghrita-nasya","name":"Cow's ghee nasal drops (Gau ghrita nasya)","nameHi":"गौ घृत नस्य (नाक में गाय का घी)","form":"Ghee","howUsed":"nasal drops","caution":"Little safety research exists; avoid in pregnancy and check with a doctor if you take regular medicines. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"occasional-tension-type-headache--shadbindu-taila","name":"Shadbindu taila","nameHi":"षड्बिंदु तैल","form":"Oil","howUsed":"nasal drops","caution":"Nasal drops: use only as advised, not for young children, and not during a nosebleed or sinus infection with fever. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"occasional-tension-type-headache--dashamoola-taila-scalp-massage","name":"Dashamoola taila (scalp massage)","nameHi":"दशमूल तैल (सिर की मालिश)","form":"Oil","howUsed":"external massage","caution":"For external use only; stop if the skin becomes irritated. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."}]},{"id":"occasional-lower-back-stiffness-or-ache","title":"Occasional lower-back stiffness or ache","titleHi":"कभी-कभी कमर में जकड़न या दर्द","otcMedicinesUsuallyUsed":"Ibuprofen, naproxen, diclofenac gel, methyl salicylate rubs","seeADoctorIf":"numbness, leg weakness, loss of bladder or bowel control, fever, or pain after a fall","source":"Ministry of AYUSH, Ayurvedic Standard Treatment Guidelines (2017), Katigraha, Table 28.1. https://main.ayush.gov.in/ayurvedic-standard-treatment-guidelines/","options":[{"id":"occasional-lower-back-stiffness-or-ache--yogaraja-guggulu","name":"Yogaraja guggulu","nameHi":"योगराज गुग्गुलु","form":"Tablet","howUsed":"internal","caution":"Guggulu: avoid in pregnancy; may interact with BP and thyroid medicines. Buy from a licensed maker (heavy-metal contamination has been found in some products). Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"occasional-lower-back-stiffness-or-ache--simhanada-guggulu","name":"Simhanada guggulu","nameHi":"सिंहनाद गुग्गुलु","form":"Tablet","howUsed":"internal","caution":"Guggulu: avoid in pregnancy; may interact with BP and thyroid medicines. Buy from a licensed maker (heavy-metal contamination has been found in some products). Laxative. Not for long-term use, children or pregnancy without a doctor's advice. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"occasional-lower-back-stiffness-or-ache--rasnasaptakam-kashaya","name":"Rasnasaptakam kashaya","nameHi":"रास्नासप्तकम् कषाय","form":"Decoction","howUsed":"internal","caution":"Little safety research exists; avoid in pregnancy and check with a doctor if you take regular medicines. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"occasional-lower-back-stiffness-or-ache--dashamoola-kashaya","name":"Dashamoola kashaya","nameHi":"दशमूल कषाय","form":"Decoction","howUsed":"internal","caution":"Little safety research exists; avoid in pregnancy and check with a doctor if you take regular medicines. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"occasional-lower-back-stiffness-or-ache--rasna-churna","name":"Rasna churna","nameHi":"रास्ना चूर्ण","form":"Powder","howUsed":"internal","caution":"Little safety research exists; avoid in pregnancy and check with a doctor if you take regular medicines. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"occasional-lower-back-stiffness-or-ache--ashwagandha-churna-with-pippalimoola-churna","name":"Ashwagandha churna with Pippalimoola churna","nameHi":"अश्वगंधा चूर्ण के साथ पिप्पलीमूल चूर्ण","form":"Powder","howUsed":"internal","caution":"Ashwagandha: avoid in pregnancy, thyroid or autoimmune conditions, and before surgery; rare liver injury reported. Contains pepper/long pepper (piperine), which can change blood levels of many prescription medicines. Ask a pharmacist if you take any. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"occasional-lower-back-stiffness-or-ache--shunthi-churna","name":"Shunthi churna","nameHi":"शुंठी चूर्ण (सोंठ)","form":"Powder","howUsed":"internal","caution":"Ginger may add to the effect of blood thinners. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"occasional-lower-back-stiffness-or-ache--murivenna-dhanwantharam-taila-nirgundyadi-taila-bala-taila","name":"Murivenna / Dhanwantharam taila / Nirgundyadi taila / Bala taila","nameHi":"मुरिवेण्णा / धन्वंतरम् तैल / निर्गुंड्यादि तैल / बला तैल","form":"Oil","howUsed":"external massage","caution":"For external use only; stop if the skin becomes irritated. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"occasional-lower-back-stiffness-or-ache--saptasaram-kashaya","name":"Saptasaram kashaya","nameHi":"सप्तसारम् कषाय","form":"Decoction","howUsed":"internal","caution":"Little safety research exists; avoid in pregnancy and check with a doctor if you take regular medicines. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"occasional-lower-back-stiffness-or-ache--soubhagya-shunthi-paka","name":"Soubhagya shunthi paka","nameHi":"सौभाग्य शुंठी पाक","form":"Herbal jam (avaleha)","howUsed":"internal","caution":"Ginger may add to the effect of blood thinners. About half sugar by weight; count it if you watch blood sugar. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"occasional-lower-back-stiffness-or-ache--guggulu-tiktaka-ghrita","name":"Guggulu tiktaka ghrita","nameHi":"गुग्गुलु तिक्तक घृत","form":"Medicated ghee","howUsed":"internal","caution":"Guggulu: avoid in pregnancy; may interact with BP and thyroid medicines. Buy from a licensed maker (heavy-metal contamination has been found in some products). Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"occasional-lower-back-stiffness-or-ache--abhayarishta","name":"Abhayarishta","nameHi":"अभयारिष्ट","form":"Arishta (liquid)","howUsed":"internal","caution":"Contains natural alcohol (arishta, about 5–13%). Avoid in pregnancy, with liver disease, before driving, and with metronidazole/tinidazole. Laxative. Not for long-term use, children or pregnancy without a doctor's advice. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"occasional-lower-back-stiffness-or-ache--balarishta","name":"Balarishta","nameHi":"बलारिष्ट","form":"Arishta (liquid)","howUsed":"internal","caution":"Contains natural alcohol (arishta, about 5–13%). Avoid in pregnancy, with liver disease, before driving, and with metronidazole/tinidazole. Contains bala (Sida cordifolia), which can contain ephedrine-like compounds: avoid with high BP, heart problems, MAOI antidepressants and in pregnancy. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"occasional-lower-back-stiffness-or-ache--dhanwantaram-taila-101-avarti-oral-drops","name":"Dhanwantaram taila (101 avarti, oral drops)","nameHi":"धन्वंतरम् तैल (101 आवर्ती, मुंह से बूंदें)","form":"Oil","howUsed":"internal (drops)","caution":"Contains bala (Sida cordifolia), which can contain ephedrine-like compounds: avoid with high BP, heart problems, MAOI antidepressants and in pregnancy. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"occasional-lower-back-stiffness-or-ache--karpasasthyadi-taila","name":"Karpasasthyadi taila","nameHi":"कार्पासास्थ्यादि तैल","form":"Oil","howUsed":"external massage","caution":"For external use only; stop if the skin becomes irritated. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"occasional-lower-back-stiffness-or-ache--prasarini-taila","name":"Prasarini taila","nameHi":"प्रसारिणी तैल","form":"Oil","howUsed":"external massage","caution":"For external use only; stop if the skin becomes irritated. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"occasional-lower-back-stiffness-or-ache--ksheerabala-taila","name":"Ksheerabala taila","nameHi":"क्षीरबला तैल","form":"Oil","howUsed":"external massage","caution":"For external use only; stop if the skin becomes irritated. Contains bala (Sida cordifolia), which can contain ephedrine-like compounds: avoid with high BP, heart problems, MAOI antidepressants and in pregnancy. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."}]},{"id":"occasional-joint-stiffness-massage-oils","title":"Occasional joint stiffness (massage oils)","titleHi":"कभी-कभी जोड़ों में जकड़न (मालिश तेल)","otcMedicinesUsuallyUsed":"Diclofenac gel, methyl salicylate / menthol rubs","seeADoctorIf":"a hot, red or swollen joint, fever, or stiffness lasting all morning","source":"Ministry of AYUSH, Ayurvedic Standard Treatment Guidelines (2017), Sandhigata vata, Table 31.1 (local application). https://main.ayush.gov.in/ayurvedic-standard-treatment-guidelines/","options":[{"id":"occasional-joint-stiffness-massage-oils--mahanarayana-taila","name":"Mahanarayana taila","nameHi":"महानारायण तैल","form":"Oil","howUsed":"external massage","caution":"For external use only; stop if the skin becomes irritated. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"occasional-joint-stiffness-massage-oils--bala-taila","name":"Bala taila","nameHi":"बला तैल","form":"Oil","howUsed":"external massage","caution":"For external use only; stop if the skin becomes irritated. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"occasional-joint-stiffness-massage-oils--sahachara-taila","name":"Sahachara taila","nameHi":"सहचर तैल","form":"Oil","howUsed":"external massage","caution":"For external use only; stop if the skin becomes irritated. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"occasional-joint-stiffness-massage-oils--nirgundi-taila","name":"Nirgundi taila","nameHi":"निर्गुंडी तैल","form":"Oil","howUsed":"external massage","caution":"For external use only; stop if the skin becomes irritated. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"occasional-joint-stiffness-massage-oils--dhanvantara-taila","name":"Dhanvantara taila","nameHi":"धन्वंतर तैल","form":"Oil","howUsed":"external massage","caution":"For external use only; stop if the skin becomes irritated. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"occasional-joint-stiffness-massage-oils--kottamchukkadi-taila","name":"Kottamchukkadi taila","nameHi":"कोट्टमचुक्कादि तैल","form":"Oil","howUsed":"external massage","caution":"For external use only; stop if the skin becomes irritated. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"occasional-joint-stiffness-massage-oils--masha-taila","name":"Masha taila","nameHi":"माष तैल","form":"Oil","howUsed":"external massage","caution":"For external use only; stop if the skin becomes irritated. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"occasional-joint-stiffness-massage-oils--ksheerabala-taila","name":"Ksheerabala taila","nameHi":"क्षीरबला तैल","form":"Oil","howUsed":"external massage","caution":"For external use only; stop if the skin becomes irritated. Contains bala (Sida cordifolia), which can contain ephedrine-like compounds: avoid with high BP, heart problems, MAOI antidepressants and in pregnancy. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"occasional-joint-stiffness-massage-oils--ashwagandha-balalakshadi-taila","name":"Ashwagandha balalakshadi taila","nameHi":"अश्वगंधा बलालाक्षादि तैल","form":"Oil","howUsed":"external massage","caution":"For external use only; stop if the skin becomes irritated. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"occasional-joint-stiffness-massage-oils--prabhanjana-vimardana-taila","name":"Prabhanjana vimardana taila","nameHi":"प्रभंजन विमर्दन तैल","form":"Oil","howUsed":"external massage","caution":"For external use only; stop if the skin becomes irritated. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"occasional-joint-stiffness-massage-oils--dashanga-lepa","name":"Dashanga lepa","nameHi":"दशांग लेप","form":"Paste","howUsed":"external paste","caution":"For external use only; stop if the skin becomes irritated. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"occasional-joint-stiffness-massage-oils--kaishora-guggulu","name":"Kaishora guggulu","nameHi":"कैशोर गुग्गुलु","form":"Tablet","howUsed":"internal","caution":"Guggulu: avoid in pregnancy; may interact with BP and thyroid medicines. Buy from a licensed maker (heavy-metal contamination has been found in some products). Laxative. Not for long-term use, children or pregnancy without a doctor's advice. Giloy (guduchi): liver injury has been reported; avoid with liver or autoimmune conditions. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"occasional-joint-stiffness-massage-oils--dashamoolarishta","name":"Dashamoolarishta","nameHi":"दशमूलारिष्ट","form":"Arishta (liquid)","howUsed":"internal","caution":"Contains natural alcohol (arishta, about 5–13%). Avoid in pregnancy, with liver disease, before driving, and with metronidazole/tinidazole. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"occasional-joint-stiffness-massage-oils--ashwagandharishta","name":"Ashwagandharishta","nameHi":"अश्वगंधारिष्ट","form":"Arishta (liquid)","howUsed":"internal","caution":"Contains natural alcohol (arishta, about 5–13%). Avoid in pregnancy, with liver disease, before driving, and with metronidazole/tinidazole. Ashwagandha: avoid in pregnancy, thyroid or autoimmune conditions, and before surgery; rare liver injury reported. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."}]},{"id":"occasional-trouble-sleeping","title":"Occasional trouble sleeping","titleHi":"कभी-कभी नींद न आना","otcMedicinesUsuallyUsed":"Diphenhydramine, doxylamine, melatonin","seeADoctorIf":"trouble sleeping most nights for more than 4 weeks, loud snoring with pauses, or low mood","source":"Ministry of AYUSH, Ayurvedic Standard Treatment Guidelines (2017), Anidra, Table 18.1. https://main.ayush.gov.in/ayurvedic-standard-treatment-guidelines/","options":[{"id":"occasional-trouble-sleeping--ashwagandhadi-churna-with-milk-at-bedtime","name":"Ashwagandhadi churna (with milk at bedtime)","nameHi":"अश्वगंधादि चूर्ण (रात को दूध के साथ)","form":"Powder","howUsed":"internal","caution":"Ashwagandha: avoid in pregnancy, thyroid or autoimmune conditions, and before surgery; rare liver injury reported. May add to drowsiness from sleeping pills, alcohol or antihistamines. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"occasional-trouble-sleeping--tagara-churna","name":"Tagara churna","nameHi":"तगर चूर्ण","form":"Powder","howUsed":"internal","caution":"May add to drowsiness from sleeping pills, alcohol or antihistamines. Little safety research exists; avoid in pregnancy and check with a doctor if you take regular medicines. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"occasional-trouble-sleeping--jatiphala-churna-nutmeg","name":"Jatiphala churna (nutmeg)","nameHi":"जातीफल चूर्ण (जायफल)","form":"Powder","howUsed":"internal","caution":"Nutmeg is toxic in large amounts; keep strictly to the advised dose and away from children. May add to drowsiness from sleeping pills, alcohol or antihistamines. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"occasional-trouble-sleeping--pippalimula-churna","name":"Pippalimula churna","nameHi":"पिप्पलीमूल चूर्ण","form":"Powder","howUsed":"internal","caution":"Contains pepper/long pepper (piperine), which can change blood levels of many prescription medicines. Ask a pharmacist if you take any. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"occasional-trouble-sleeping--saraswata-churna","name":"Saraswata churna","nameHi":"सारस्वत चूर्ण","form":"Powder","howUsed":"internal","caution":"May add to drowsiness from sleeping pills, alcohol or antihistamines. Little safety research exists; avoid in pregnancy and check with a doctor if you take regular medicines. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"occasional-trouble-sleeping--mamsyadi-kwatha","name":"Mamsyadi kwatha","nameHi":"मांस्यादि क्वाथ","form":"Decoction","howUsed":"internal","caution":"Jatamansi is calming; may add to drowsiness from sleeping pills or alcohol. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"occasional-trouble-sleeping--drakshadi-kwatha","name":"Drakshadi kwatha","nameHi":"द्राक्षादि क्वाथ","form":"Decoction","howUsed":"internal","caution":"Little safety research exists; avoid in pregnancy and check with a doctor if you take regular medicines. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"occasional-trouble-sleeping--brahmi-ghrita-nasal-drops","name":"Brahmi ghrita (nasal drops)","nameHi":"ब्राह्मी घृत (नाक में बूंदें)","form":"Medicated ghee","howUsed":"nasal drops","caution":"Nasal drops: use only as advised, not for young children, and not during a nosebleed or sinus infection with fever. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"occasional-trouble-sleeping--ksheerabala-taila-head-application","name":"Ksheerabala taila (head application)","nameHi":"क्षीरबला तैल (सिर पर लगाने के लिए)","form":"Oil","howUsed":"external (scalp)","caution":"For external use only; stop if the skin becomes irritated. Contains bala (Sida cordifolia), which can contain ephedrine-like compounds: avoid with high BP, heart problems, MAOI antidepressants and in pregnancy. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"occasional-trouble-sleeping--chandanadi-taila-head-application","name":"Chandanadi taila (head application)","nameHi":"चंदनादि तैल (सिर पर लगाने के लिए)","form":"Oil","howUsed":"external (scalp)","caution":"For external use only; stop if the skin becomes irritated. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."}]},{"id":"mouth-ulcers-minor","title":"Mouth ulcers (minor)","titleHi":"मुंह के छाले (हल्के)","otcMedicinesUsuallyUsed":"Choline salicylate gel, benzocaine gel, antiseptic mouthwash","seeADoctorIf":"an ulcer lasting more than 3 weeks, a painless white or red patch, or ulcers with fever","source":"Ministry of AYUSH, Ayurvedic Standard Treatment Guidelines (2017), Mukhapaka, Table 36.1. https://main.ayush.gov.in/ayurvedic-standard-treatment-guidelines/","options":[{"id":"mouth-ulcers-minor--honey-gargle-kshaudra","name":"Honey gargle (kshaudra)","nameHi":"शहद से कुल्ला (क्षौद्र)","form":"Liquid","howUsed":"gargle","caution":"No specific caution found; avoid in pregnancy unless a doctor advises. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"mouth-ulcers-minor--jatipatra-jasmine-leaf-paste","name":"Jatipatra (jasmine leaf) paste","nameHi":"जातीपत्र (चमेली की पत्ती) का लेप","form":"Paste","howUsed":"apply in mouth","caution":"Apply in the mouth only; do not swallow large amounts. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"mouth-ulcers-minor--yashtimadhu-churna-with-gairika-in-honey-and-ghee","name":"Yashtimadhu churna with Gairika, in honey and ghee","nameHi":"यष्टिमधु चूर्ण के साथ गैरिक, शहद और घी में","form":"Powder","howUsed":"apply in mouth","caution":"Apply in the mouth only; do not swallow large amounts. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"mouth-ulcers-minor--darvighana-with-gairika","name":"Darvighana with Gairika","nameHi":"दार्वीघन के साथ गैरिक","form":"Powder","howUsed":"apply in mouth","caution":"Apply in the mouth only; do not swallow large amounts. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"mouth-ulcers-minor--samshamani-vati-guduchi","name":"Samshamani vati (guduchi)","nameHi":"संशमनी वटी (गुडूची / गिलोय)","form":"Tablet","howUsed":"internal","caution":"Giloy (guduchi): liver injury has been reported; avoid with liver or autoimmune conditions. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"mouth-ulcers-minor--swadishta-virechana-churna","name":"Swadishta virechana churna","nameHi":"स्वादिष्ट विरेचन चूर्ण","form":"Powder","howUsed":"internal (at night)","caution":"Senna-based laxative. Not in pregnancy, breastfeeding or under 12; not for long-term use. Contains licorice (mulethi): can raise blood pressure and lower potassium. Avoid with BP or heart medicines, water tablets, steroids, and in pregnancy. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"mouth-ulcers-minor--triphala-kwatha-gargle","name":"Triphala kwatha gargle","nameHi":"त्रिफला क्वाथ से कुल्ला","form":"Decoction","howUsed":"gargle","caution":"Apply in the mouth only; do not swallow large amounts. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"mouth-ulcers-minor--panchavalkala-kwatha-gargle","name":"Panchavalkala kwatha gargle","nameHi":"पंचवल्कल क्वाथ से कुल्ला","form":"Decoction","howUsed":"gargle","caution":"Apply in the mouth only; do not swallow large amounts. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"mouth-ulcers-minor--panchapallava-kwatha-gargle","name":"Panchapallava kwatha gargle","nameHi":"पंचपल्लव क्वाथ से कुल्ला","form":"Decoction","howUsed":"gargle","caution":"Apply in the mouth only; do not swallow large amounts. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"mouth-ulcers-minor--panchatikta-kwatha-gargle","name":"Panchatikta kwatha gargle","nameHi":"पंचतिक्त क्वाथ से कुल्ला","form":"Decoction","howUsed":"gargle","caution":"Apply in the mouth only; do not swallow large amounts. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"mouth-ulcers-minor--khadiradi-gutika","name":"Khadiradi gutika","nameHi":"खदिरादि गुटिका","form":"Tablet","howUsed":"rub on gums / suck","caution":"Apply in the mouth only; do not swallow large amounts. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."}]},{"id":"intestinal-worms-adults","title":"Intestinal worms (adults)","titleHi":"पेट के कीड़े (वयस्क)","otcMedicinesUsuallyUsed":"Albendazole, mebendazole","seeADoctorIf":"worms seen in stool with weight loss, a child under 2, pregnancy, or symptoms after treatment","source":"Ministry of AYUSH, Ayurvedic Standard Treatment Guidelines (2017), Krimi, Tables 16.1–16.2. https://main.ayush.gov.in/ayurvedic-standard-treatment-guidelines/","options":[{"id":"intestinal-worms-adults--vidangadi-churna","name":"Vidangadi churna","nameHi":"विडंगादि चूर्ण","form":"Powder","howUsed":"internal","caution":"For children, ask a doctor first; India's national deworming programme uses albendazole. Little safety research exists; avoid in pregnancy and check with a doctor if you take regular medicines. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"intestinal-worms-adults--nimbadi-churna","name":"Nimbadi churna","nameHi":"निंबादि चूर्ण","form":"Powder","howUsed":"internal","caution":"For children, ask a doctor first; India's national deworming programme uses albendazole. Little safety research exists; avoid in pregnancy and check with a doctor if you take regular medicines. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"intestinal-worms-adults--vidanga-avaleha","name":"Vidanga avaleha","nameHi":"विडंग अवलेह","form":"Herbal jam (avaleha)","howUsed":"internal","caution":"For children, ask a doctor first; India's national deworming programme uses albendazole. About half sugar by weight; count it if you watch blood sugar. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"intestinal-worms-adults--vidangarishta","name":"Vidangarishta","nameHi":"विडंगारिष्ट","form":"Arishta (liquid)","howUsed":"internal","caution":"For children, ask a doctor first; India's national deworming programme uses albendazole. Contains natural alcohol (arishta, about 5–13%). Avoid in pregnancy, with liver disease, before driving, and with metronidazole/tinidazole. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"intestinal-worms-adults--haridra-khanda","name":"Haridra khanda","nameHi":"हरिद्रा खंड","form":"Granules","howUsed":"internal","caution":"For children, ask a doctor first; India's national deworming programme uses albendazole. Turmeric may add to the effect of blood thinners; not in pregnancy at medicinal doses. About half sugar by weight; count it if you watch blood sugar. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."}]},{"id":"piles-discomfort","title":"Piles discomfort","titleHi":"बवासीर की तकलीफ़","otcMedicinesUsuallyUsed":"Hydrocortisone/lidocaine piles creams, stool softeners","seeADoctorIf":"any rectal bleeding (always get checked once), black stools, change in bowel habit over 40, or severe pain","source":"Ministry of AYUSH, Ayurvedic Standard Treatment Guidelines (2017), Arsha, Tables 13.2–13.3 and local application. https://main.ayush.gov.in/ayurvedic-standard-treatment-guidelines/","options":[{"id":"piles-discomfort--triphala-churna","name":"Triphala churna","nameHi":"त्रिफला चूर्ण","form":"Powder","howUsed":"internal","caution":"Laxative. Not for long-term use, children or pregnancy without a doctor's advice. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"piles-discomfort--haritaki-churna","name":"Haritaki churna","nameHi":"हरीतकी चूर्ण","form":"Powder","howUsed":"internal","caution":"Laxative. Not for long-term use, children or pregnancy without a doctor's advice. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"piles-discomfort--draksha-dried-black-raisins","name":"Draksha (dried black raisins)","nameHi":"द्राक्षा (काली किशमिश / मुनक्का)","form":"Dried fruit","howUsed":"internal","caution":"No specific caution found; avoid in pregnancy unless a doctor advises. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"piles-discomfort--phalatrikadi-kwatha","name":"Phalatrikadi kwatha","nameHi":"फलत्रिकादि क्वाथ","form":"Decoction","howUsed":"internal","caution":"Laxative. Not for long-term use, children or pregnancy without a doctor's advice. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"piles-discomfort--erandamula-kwatha","name":"Erandamula kwatha","nameHi":"एरंडमूल क्वाथ","form":"Decoction","howUsed":"internal","caution":"Little safety research exists; avoid in pregnancy and check with a doctor if you take regular medicines. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"piles-discomfort--jatyadi-taila","name":"Jatyadi taila","nameHi":"जात्यादि तैल","form":"Oil","howUsed":"external (local application)","caution":"For external use only; stop if the skin becomes irritated. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"piles-discomfort--murivenna","name":"Murivenna","nameHi":"मुरिवेण्णा","form":"Oil","howUsed":"external (local application)","caution":"For external use only; stop if the skin becomes irritated. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"piles-discomfort--triphala-kwatha-sitz-bath-avagaha","name":"Triphala kwatha sitz bath (avagaha)","nameHi":"त्रिफला क्वाथ से बैठकर स्नान (अवगाह)","form":"Decoction","howUsed":"sitz bath","caution":"For a lukewarm sitz bath only; do not drink. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"piles-discomfort--panchavalkala-kwatha-sitz-bath-avagaha","name":"Panchavalkala kwatha sitz bath (avagaha)","nameHi":"पंचवल्कल क्वाथ से बैठकर स्नान (अवगाह)","form":"Decoction","howUsed":"sitz bath","caution":"For a lukewarm sitz bath only; do not drink. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."}]},{"id":"shoulder-stiffness","title":"Shoulder stiffness","titleHi":"कंधे में जकड़न","otcMedicinesUsuallyUsed":"Ibuprofen, diclofenac gel","seeADoctorIf":"pain after a fall, pain with chest discomfort or breathlessness, fever, or inability to lift the arm","source":"Ministry of AYUSH, Ayurvedic Standard Treatment Guidelines (2017), Avabahuka, Tables 27.1–27.2. https://main.ayush.gov.in/ayurvedic-standard-treatment-guidelines/","options":[{"id":"shoulder-stiffness--ashwagandha-churna","name":"Ashwagandha churna","nameHi":"अश्वगंधा चूर्ण","form":"Powder","howUsed":"internal","caution":"Ashwagandha: avoid in pregnancy, thyroid or autoimmune conditions, and before surgery; rare liver injury reported. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"shoulder-stiffness--bala-churna","name":"Bala churna","nameHi":"बला चूर्ण","form":"Powder","howUsed":"internal","caution":"Contains bala (Sida cordifolia), which can contain ephedrine-like compounds: avoid with high BP, heart problems, MAOI antidepressants and in pregnancy. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"shoulder-stiffness--rasna-churna","name":"Rasna churna","nameHi":"रास्ना चूर्ण","form":"Powder","howUsed":"internal","caution":"Little safety research exists; avoid in pregnancy and check with a doctor if you take regular medicines. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"shoulder-stiffness--chopchini-churna","name":"Chopchini churna","nameHi":"चोपचीनी चूर्ण","form":"Powder","howUsed":"internal","caution":"Little safety research exists; avoid in pregnancy and check with a doctor if you take regular medicines. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"shoulder-stiffness--dashamoola-kashaya","name":"Dashamoola kashaya","nameHi":"दशमूल कषाय","form":"Decoction","howUsed":"internal","caution":"Little safety research exists; avoid in pregnancy and check with a doctor if you take regular medicines. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"shoulder-stiffness--yogaraja-guggulu","name":"Yogaraja guggulu","nameHi":"योगराज गुग्गुलु","form":"Tablet","howUsed":"internal","caution":"Guggulu: avoid in pregnancy; may interact with BP and thyroid medicines. Buy from a licensed maker (heavy-metal contamination has been found in some products). Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"shoulder-stiffness--guggulu-tiktakam-kwatha","name":"Guggulu tiktakam kwatha","nameHi":"गुग्गुलु तिक्तकम् क्वाथ","form":"Decoction","howUsed":"internal","caution":"Guggulu: avoid in pregnancy; may interact with BP and thyroid medicines. Buy from a licensed maker (heavy-metal contamination has been found in some products). Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"shoulder-stiffness--prasaranyadi-kashaya","name":"Prasaranyadi kashaya","nameHi":"प्रसारण्यादि कषाय","form":"Decoction","howUsed":"internal","caution":"Little safety research exists; avoid in pregnancy and check with a doctor if you take regular medicines. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"shoulder-stiffness--maharasnadi-kwatha","name":"Maharasnadi kwatha","nameHi":"महारास्नादि क्वाथ","form":"Decoction","howUsed":"internal","caution":"Little safety research exists; avoid in pregnancy and check with a doctor if you take regular medicines. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"shoulder-stiffness--vidaryadi-kwatha","name":"Vidaryadi kwatha","nameHi":"विदार्यादि क्वाथ","form":"Decoction","howUsed":"internal","caution":"Little safety research exists; avoid in pregnancy and check with a doctor if you take regular medicines. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"shoulder-stiffness--dhanwantharam-kwatha","name":"Dhanwantharam kwatha","nameHi":"धन्वंतरम् क्वाथ","form":"Decoction","howUsed":"internal","caution":"Contains bala (Sida cordifolia), which can contain ephedrine-like compounds: avoid with high BP, heart problems, MAOI antidepressants and in pregnancy. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"shoulder-stiffness--balarishta","name":"Balarishta","nameHi":"बलारिष्ट","form":"Arishta (liquid)","howUsed":"internal","caution":"Contains natural alcohol (arishta, about 5–13%). Avoid in pregnancy, with liver disease, before driving, and with metronidazole/tinidazole. Contains bala (Sida cordifolia), which can contain ephedrine-like compounds: avoid with high BP, heart problems, MAOI antidepressants and in pregnancy. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"shoulder-stiffness--anu-taila","name":"Anu taila","nameHi":"अणु तैल","form":"Oil","howUsed":"nasal drops","caution":"Nasal drops: use only as advised, not for young children, and not during a nosebleed or sinus infection with fever. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"shoulder-stiffness--karpasasthyadi-taila","name":"Karpasasthyadi taila","nameHi":"कार्पासास्थ्यादि तैल","form":"Oil","howUsed":"external massage","caution":"For external use only; stop if the skin becomes irritated. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"shoulder-stiffness--nirgundi-taila","name":"Nirgundi taila","nameHi":"निर्गुंडी तैल","form":"Oil","howUsed":"external massage","caution":"For external use only; stop if the skin becomes irritated. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"shoulder-stiffness--parinata-keryadi-taila","name":"Parinata keryadi taila","nameHi":"परिणत केर्यादि तैल","form":"Oil","howUsed":"external massage","caution":"For external use only; stop if the skin becomes irritated. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."}]},{"id":"period-cramps","title":"Period cramps","titleHi":"मासिक धर्म का दर्द","otcMedicinesUsuallyUsed":"Mefenamic acid, ibuprofen, dicyclomine","seeADoctorIf":"pain that is severe or getting worse, very heavy bleeding, pain between periods, or a chance of pregnancy","source":"Ministry of AYUSH, Ayurvedic Standard Treatment Guidelines (2017), Kashtartava, Tables 25.1–25.2. https://main.ayush.gov.in/ayurvedic-standard-treatment-guidelines/","options":[{"id":"period-cramps--hingvadi-churna","name":"Hingvadi churna","nameHi":"हिंग्वादि चूर्ण","form":"Powder","howUsed":"internal","caution":"Contains asafoetida: not for infants or in pregnancy. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"period-cramps--hingvadi-gutika","name":"Hingvadi gutika","nameHi":"हिंग्वादि गुटिका","form":"Tablet","howUsed":"internal","caution":"Contains asafoetida: not for infants or in pregnancy. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"period-cramps--chaturbeeja-churna","name":"Chaturbeeja churna","nameHi":"चतुर्बीज चूर्ण","form":"Powder","howUsed":"internal","caution":"Contains fenugreek, which may lower blood sugar; take care with diabetes medicines. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"period-cramps--eranda-bhrishta-haritaki-with-shunthi","name":"Eranda bhrishta haritaki with shunthi","nameHi":"एरंड भृष्ट हरीतकी के साथ शुंठी","form":"Powder","howUsed":"internal","caution":"Laxative. Not for long-term use, children or pregnancy without a doctor's advice. Ginger may add to the effect of blood thinners. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"period-cramps--devadarvyadi-kwatha","name":"Devadarvyadi kwatha","nameHi":"देवदार्व्यादि क्वाथ","form":"Decoction","howUsed":"internal","caution":"Little safety research exists; avoid in pregnancy and check with a doctor if you take regular medicines. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"period-cramps--yogaraja-guggulu","name":"Yogaraja guggulu","nameHi":"योगराज गुग्गुलु","form":"Tablet","howUsed":"internal","caution":"Guggulu: avoid in pregnancy; may interact with BP and thyroid medicines. Buy from a licensed maker (heavy-metal contamination has been found in some products). Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"period-cramps--mahanarayana-taila","name":"Mahanarayana taila","nameHi":"महानारायण तैल","form":"Oil","howUsed":"external massage (lower back/abdomen)","caution":"For external use only; stop if the skin becomes irritated. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."}]},{"id":"gum-care-sore-or-swollen-gums","title":"Gum care (sore or swollen gums)","titleHi":"मसूड़ों की देखभाल (दर्द या सूजन)","otcMedicinesUsuallyUsed":"Chlorhexidine mouthwash, antiseptic gum gels","seeADoctorIf":"gums that bleed easily without brushing, loose teeth, or swelling of the face","source":"Ministry of AYUSH, Ayurvedic Standard Treatment Guidelines (2017), Dantaveshta, Table 35.1. https://main.ayush.gov.in/ayurvedic-standard-treatment-guidelines/","options":[{"id":"gum-care-sore-or-swollen-gums--panchavalkala-kwatha","name":"Panchavalkala kwatha","nameHi":"पंचवल्कल क्वाथ","form":"Decoction","howUsed":"gargle","caution":"Apply in the mouth only; do not swallow large amounts. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"gum-care-sore-or-swollen-gums--kshiri-vriksha-kashaya","name":"Kshiri vriksha kashaya","nameHi":"क्षीरी वृक्ष कषाय","form":"Decoction","howUsed":"hold in mouth, then spit","caution":"Apply in the mouth only; do not swallow large amounts. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"gum-care-sore-or-swollen-gums--dashana-samskara-churna","name":"Dashana samskara churna","nameHi":"दशन संस्कार चूर्ण","form":"Powder","howUsed":"rub on gums","caution":"Apply in the mouth only; do not swallow large amounts. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"gum-care-sore-or-swollen-gums--kalaka-churna","name":"Kalaka churna","nameHi":"कालक चूर्ण","form":"Powder","howUsed":"rub on gums","caution":"Apply in the mouth only; do not swallow large amounts. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"gum-care-sore-or-swollen-gums--pitaka-churna","name":"Pitaka churna","nameHi":"पीतक चूर्ण","form":"Powder","howUsed":"rub on gums","caution":"Apply in the mouth only; do not swallow large amounts. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"gum-care-sore-or-swollen-gums--irimedadi-taila","name":"Irimedadi taila","nameHi":"इरिमेदादि तैल","form":"Oil","howUsed":"gum massage","caution":"Apply in the mouth only; do not swallow large amounts. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"gum-care-sore-or-swollen-gums--khadiradi-gutika","name":"Khadiradi gutika","nameHi":"खदिरादि गुटिका","form":"Tablet","howUsed":"gum massage","caution":"Apply in the mouth only; do not swallow large amounts. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."},{"id":"gum-care-sore-or-swollen-gums--triphala-guggulu","name":"Triphala guggulu","nameHi":"त्रिफला गुग्गुलु","form":"Tablet","howUsed":"internal","caution":"Guggulu: avoid in pregnancy; may interact with BP and thyroid medicines. Buy from a licensed maker (heavy-metal contamination has been found in some products). Laxative. Not for long-term use, children or pregnancy without a doctor's advice. Dose: ask a qualified Ayurvedic doctor."}]}]}
