ut","evidence":"clinical","advice":"Talk to your doctor or pharmacist before combining; check your blood sugar more often and know the signs of low blood sugar.","sources":["https://www.niaaa.nih.gov/publications/brochures-and-fact-sheets/harmful-interactions-mixing-alcohol-with-medicines","https://www.ijp-online.com/article.asp?issn=0253-7613;year=2006;volume=38;issue=5;spage=365;epage=365;aulast=Weerasooriya"],"onlyMolecules":null,"majorOnlyFor":null},{"drugClass":"antidiabetic_sulfonylurea","severity":"moderate","effect":"alcohol may cause low blood sugar or a flushing reaction with some sulfonylureas","mechanism":"via ingredient: self-generated alcohol (ethanol); alcohol impairs liver glucose output","evidence":"clinical","advice":"Talk to your doctor or pharmacist before combining; check your blood sugar more often and know the signs of low blood sugar.","sources":["https://www.niaaa.nih.gov/publications/brochures-and-fact-sheets/harmful-interactions-mixing-alcohol-with-medicines","https://www.ijp-online.com/article.asp?issn=0253-7613;year=2006;volume=38;issue=5;spage=365;epage=365;aulast=Weerasooriya"],"onlyMolecules":null,"majorOnlyFor":null},{"drugClass":"cyp3a4_substrate_narrow","severity":"moderate","effect":"may raise levels of medicines broken down by CYP3A4","mechanism":"via ingredient arjuna: extracts inhibited CYP3A4, CYP2D6 and CYP2C9 in human liver microsomes","evidence":"preclinical","advice":"Talk to your doctor or pharmacist before combining.","sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/28962416/"],"onlyMolecules":null,"majorOnlyFor":null},{"drugClass":"cyp2d6_substrate","severity":"minor","effect":"may raise levels of CYP2D6 substrates (e.g. metoprolol)","mechanism":"via ingredient arjuna (in vitro) and a related arishta formulation (CYP2D6 inhibition in vitro)","evidence":"preclinical","advice":"Talk to your doctor or pharmacist before combining.","sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/28962416/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/27457692/"],"onlyMolecules":null,"majorOnlyFor":null},{"drugClass":"cyp2c9_substrate","severity":"minor","effect":"may raise levels of CYP2C9 substrates (e.g. warfarin)","mechanism":"via ingredient arjuna: CYP2C9 inhibition in human liver microsomes","evidence":"preclinical","advice":"Talk to your doctor or pharmacist before combining.","sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/28962416/"],"onlyMolecules":null,"majorOnlyFor":null},{"drugClass":"cyp2c19_substrate","severity":"minor","effect":"may raise levels of CYP2C19 substrates (e.g. citalopram, omeprazole) or reduce activation of clopidogrel","mechanism":"related formulation (Ridayarishta, made from Arjunarishta/Ashwagandharishta ingredients) inhibited CYP2C19 in vitro","evidence":"preclinical","advice":"Talk to your doctor or pharmacist before combining.","sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/27457692/"],"onlyMolecules":null,"majorOnlyFor":null},{"drugClass":"antihypertensive","severity":"minor","effect":"may add to blood-pressure lowering","mechanism":"product studied: Arjunarishta lowered systolic blood pressure in high-fat-fed rats","evidence":"preclinical","advice":"Talk to your doctor or pharmacist before combining.","sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29249636/"],"onlyMolecules":null,"majorOnlyFor":null},{"drugClass":"antidiabetic_other","severity":"minor","effect":"may add to blood-sugar lowering","mechanism":"product studied: Arjunarishta lowered fasting blood glucose in high-fat-fed rats","evidence":"preclinical","advice":"Talk to your doctor or pharmacist before combining; check your blood sugar more often and know the signs of low blood sugar.","sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29249636/"],"onlyMolecules":null,"majorOnlyFor":null}],"herbWarnings":[]},{"id":"kumaryasava","name":"Kumaryasava","nameHi":"कुमार्यासव","sanskrit":"Kumaryasava","latin":null,"otherNames":["ingredients: kumari / aloe vera juice (Aloe barbadensis)","jaggery","honey","dhataki flowers","about 40-50 crude drugs","some classical recipes include iron (loha) preparations - check label","class: asava (self-fermented, alcohol-containing)"],"kind":"formulation","dataQuality":"poor","traditionalContext":"A fermented aloe-based tonic traditionally used in Ayurveda for general wellbeing of the digestive and female reproductive systems.","isAyurvedic":true,"commonProducts":["Baidyanath Kumaryasava","Dabur Kumaryasava","Kumaryasava No.1"],"safetyFlags":[{"flag":"other","note":"Contains self-generated alcohol from fermentation (arishta/asava). Tested commercial arishtas contained roughly 5-13% v/v ethanol; levels vary by brand and batch. Kumaryasava brands measured only 0.1-1.9% v/v in one gas-chromatography study, lower than other arishtas. People who must avoid alcohol should ask a doctor or pharmacist.","evidence":"clinical","sources":["https://www.niaaa.nih.gov/publications/brochures-and-fact-sheets/harmful-interactions-mixing-alcohol-with-medicines","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/25767329/"]}],"interactions":[{"drugClass":"antibiotic_other","severity":"moderate","effect":"alcohol with metronidazole or tinidazole may cause flushing, vomiting, fast heartbeat and blood-pressure changes","mechanism":"via ingredient: self-generated alcohol (ethanol); disulfiram-like reaction with nitroimidazole antibiotics","evidence":"clinical","advice":"Avoid alcohol-containing products while taking metronidazole/tinidazole unless your doctor says otherwise; talk to your doctor or pharmacist.","sources":["https://www.niaaa.nih.gov/publications/brochures-and-fact-sheets/harmful-interactions-mixing-alcohol-with-medicines","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/25767329/"],"onlyMolecules":["metronidazole","ornidazole","secnidazole","tinidazole"],"majorOnlyFor":null},{"drugClass":"sedative_hypnotic","severity":"minor","effect":"may increase drowsiness, dizziness and slowed breathing","mechanism":"via ingredient: self-generated alcohol (ethanol); additive central nervous system depression","evidence":"clinical","advice":"Talk to your doctor or pharmacist before combining.","sources":["https://www.niaaa.nih.gov/publications/brochures-and-fact-sheets/harmful-interactions-mixing-alcohol-with-medicines","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/25767329/"],"onlyMolecules":null,"majorOnlyFor":null},{"drugClass":"opioid","severity":"minor","effect":"may increase drowsiness and the risk of slowed breathing or overdose","mechanism":"via ingredient: self-generated alcohol (ethanol); additive central nervous system depression","evidence":"clinical","advice":"Talk to your doctor or pharmacist before combining.","sources":["https://www.niaaa.nih.gov/publications/brochures-and-fact-sheets/harmful-interactions-mixing-alcohol-with-medicines","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/25767329/"],"onlyMolecules":null,"majorOnlyFor":null},{"drugClass":"antiepileptic","severity":"minor","effect":"may increase drowsiness and dizziness with seizure medicines","mechanism":"via ingredient: self-generated alcohol (ethanol); additive sedation","evidence":"clinical","advice":"Talk to your doctor or pharmacist before combining.","sources":["https://www.niaaa.nih.gov/publications/brochures-and-fact-sheets/harmful-interactions-mixing-alcohol-with-medicines","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/25767329/"],"onlyMolecules":null,"majorOnlyFor":null},{"drugClass":"antidiabetic_insulin","severity":"minor","effect":"alcohol may cause low blood sugar with insulin","mechanism":"via ingredient: self-generated alcohol (ethanol); alcohol impairs liver glucose output","evidence":"clinical","advice":"Talk to your doctor or pharmacist before combining; check your blood sugar more often and know the signs of low blood sugar.","sources":["https://www.niaaa.nih.gov/publications/brochures-and-fact-sheets/harmful-interactions-mixing-alcohol-with-medicines","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/25767329/"],"onlyMolecules":null,"majorOnlyFor":null},{"drugClass":"antidiabetic_sulfonylurea","severity":"minor","effect":"alcohol may cause low blood sugar or a flushing reaction with some sulfonylureas","mechanism":"via ingredient: self-generated alcohol (ethanol); alcohol impairs liver glucose output","evidence":"clinical","advice":"Talk to your doctor or pharmacist before combining; check your blood sugar more often and know the signs of low blood sugar.","sources":["https://www.niaaa.nih.gov/publications/brochures-and-fact-sheets/harmful-interactions-mixing-alcohol-with-medicines","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/25767329/"],"onlyMolecules":null,"majorOnlyFor":null},{"drugClass":"antidiabetic_other","severity":"minor","effect":"may affect blood sugar with diabetes medicines","mechanism":"via ingredient aloe: NCCIH cautions that aloe with diabetes drugs can cause unwanted effects","evidence":"theoretical","advice":"Talk to your doctor or pharmacist before combining; check your blood sugar more often and know the signs of low blood sugar.","sources":["https://www.nccih.nih.gov/health/diabetes-and-dietary-supplements-what-you-need-to-know"],"onlyMolecules":null,"majorOnlyFor":null},{"drugClass":"cardiac_glycoside","severity":"minor","effect":"theoretical risk of low potassium with digoxin","mechanism":"via ingredient aloe: aloe latex overuse can lower potassium and raise digoxin risk; Kumaryasava uses juice, not latex (theoretical)","evidence":"theoretical","advice":"Talk to your doctor or pharmacist before combining.","sources":["https://www.nccih.nih.gov/health/aloe-vera"],"onlyMolecules":null,"majorOnlyFor":null}],"herbWarnings":[]},{"id":"kaishore_guggulu","name":"Kaishore guggulu","nameHi":"कैशोर गुग्गुलु","sanskrit":"Kaishora guggulu","latin":null,"otherNames":["ingredients: guggulu (Commiphora wightii resin)","triphala (amla, haritaki, bibhitaki)","guduchi / giloy (Tinospora cordifolia)","trikatu (ginger, black pepper, long pepper)","vidanga","danti (Baliospermum montanum)","trivrit (Operculina turpethum)"],"kind":"formulation","dataQuality":"limited","traditionalContext":"A guggul-based tablet traditionally used in Ayurveda for general wellbeing of the joints and skin.","isAyurvedic":true,"commonProducts":["Baidyanath Kaishore guggulu","Dabur Kaishore guggulu","Patanjali Divya Kaishore guggulu"],"safetyFlags":[{"flag":"liver","note":"Contains guduchi (giloy); giloy products were linked to liver injury in an Indian multicentre study (disputed by the Ministry of AYUSH).","evidence":"case_reports","sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/35037744/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34230786/","https://www.pib.gov.in/PressReleasePage.aspx?PRID=1733260"]}],"interactions":[{"drugClass":"antihypertensive","severity":"moderate","effect":"may lower the effect of propranolol and diltiazem","mechanism":"via ingredient guggulu (Commiphora wightii): single-dose study in healthy volunteers showed reduced Cmax and AUC of propranolol and diltiazem","evidence":"clinical","advice":"Talk to your doctor or pharmacist before combining; your blood pressure or heart rate may need checking.","sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/7852226/"],"onlyMolecules":null,"majorOnlyFor":null},{"drugClass":"cyp3a4_substrate_narrow","severity":"moderate","effect":"may change levels of medicines broken down by CYP3A4","mechanism":"via ingredient guggulu (Commiphora wightii): guggulsterone activates PXR and induces CYP3A in hepatocytes (lab studies)","evidence":"preclinical","advice":"Talk to your doctor or pharmacist before combining.","sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15075359/","https://www.mskcc.org/cancer-care/integrative-medicine/herbs/guggul"],"onlyMolecules":null,"majorOnlyFor":null},{"drugClass":"hormonal_contraceptive_estrogen","severity":"minor","effect":"theoretical interference with hormonal medicines","mechanism":"via ingredient guggulu (Commiphora wightii): guggulsterone activated estrogen and progesterone receptors in vitro (theoretical)","evidence":"theoretical","advice":"Talk to your doctor or pharmacist before combining.","sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15075359/"],"onlyMolecules":null,"majorOnlyFor":null},{"drugClass":"antiepileptic","severity":"minor","effect":"may raise blood levels of phenytoin","mechanism":"via ingredient trikatu (black pepper, long pepper) (piperine): increased phenytoin AUC and Cmax in patients with epilepsy","evidence":"clinical","advice":"Talk to your doctor or pharmacist before combining.","sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/16767797/"],"onlyMolecules":null,"majorOnlyFor":null},{"drugClass":"theophylline","severity":"minor","effect":"may raise blood levels of theophylline","mechanism":"via ingredient trikatu (black pepper, long pepper) (piperine): increased oral bioavailability of theophylline in healthy volunteers","evidence":"clinical","advice":"Talk to your doctor or pharmacist before combining.","sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/1815977/"],"onlyMolecules":null,"majorOnlyFor":null},{"drugClass":"laxative_stimulant","severity":"minor","effect":"may add to laxative effect","mechanism":"via ingredients triphala, danti and trivrit (laxative/purgative herbs); product unstudied","evidence":"theoretical","advice":"Talk to your doctor or pharmacist before combining.","sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/28696777/"],"onlyMolecules":null,"majorOnlyFor":null}],"herbWarnings":[]},{"id":"yogaraj_guggulu","name":"Yogaraj guggulu","nameHi":"योगराज गुग्गुलु","sanskrit":"Yogaraja guggulu","latin":null,"otherNames":["ingredients: guggulu (Commiphora wightii resin)","triphala","trikatu","chitrak (Plumbago zeylanica)","pippalimool","ajwain","vidanga","devdaru","rasna","gokshura","jeera","musta","ela","tvak"],"kind":"formulation","dataQuality":"limited","traditionalContext":"A guggul-based multi-herb tablet traditionally used in Ayurveda for general wellbeing of the joints and musculoskeletal system.","isAyurvedic":true,"commonProducts":["Baidyanath Yogaraj guggulu","Dabur Yogaraj guggulu","Patanjali Divya Yograj guggulu"],"safetyFlags":[{"flag":"heavy_metals","note":"Classical Yogaraj guggulu is herbal, but heavy metals have been found in a share of Ayurvedic products, and the related Mahayogaraj guggulu contains metal bhasmas. Do not confuse the two; choose tested products.","evidence":"regulatory","sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15598918/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/18728265/","https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/preview/mmwrhtml/mm5326a3.htm","https://www.fda.gov/drugs/fraudulent-products/fda-warns-about-heavy-metal-poisoning-associated-certain-unapproved-ayurvedic-drug-products"]}],"interactions":[{"drugClass":"antihypertensive","severity":"moderate","effect":"may lower the effect of propranolol and diltiazem","mechanism":"via ingredient guggulu (Commiphora wightii): single-dose study in healthy volunteers showed reduced Cmax and AUC of propranolol and diltiazem","evidence":"clinical","advice":"Talk to your doctor or pharmacist before combining; your blood pressure or heart rate may need checking.","sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/7852226/"],"onlyMolecules":null,"majorOnlyFor":null},{"drugClass":"cyp3a4_substrate_narrow","severity":"moderate","effect":"may change levels of medicines broken down by CYP3A4","mechanism":"via ingredient guggulu (Commiphora wightii): guggulsterone activates PXR and induces CYP3A in hepatocytes (lab studies)","evidence":"preclinical","advice":"Talk to your doctor or pharmacist before combining.","sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15075359/","https://www.mskcc.org/cancer-care/integrative-medicine/herbs/guggul"],"onlyMolecules":null,"majorOnlyFor":null},{"drugClass":"hormonal_contraceptive_estrogen","severity":"minor","effect":"theoretical interference with hormonal medicines","mechanism":"via ingredient guggulu (Commiphora wightii): guggulsterone activated estrogen and progesterone receptors in vitro (theoretical)","evidence":"theoretical","advice":"Talk to your doctor or pharmacist before combining.","sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15075359/"],"onlyMolecules":null,"majorOnlyFor":null},{"drugClass":"antiepileptic","severity":"minor","effect":"may raise blood levels of phenytoin","mechanism":"via ingredient trikatu (black pepper, long pepper) (piperine): increased phenytoin AUC and Cmax in patients with epilepsy","evidence":"clinical","advice":"Talk to your doctor or pharmacist before combining.","sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/16767797/"],"onlyMolecules":null,"majorOnlyFor":null},{"drugClass":"theophylline","severity":"minor","effect":"may raise blood levels of theophylline","mechanism":"via ingredient trikatu (black pepper, long pepper) (piperine): increased oral bioavailability of theophylline in healthy volunteers","evidence":"clinical","advice":"Talk to your doctor or pharmacist before combining.","sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/1815977/"],"onlyMolecules":null,"majorOnlyFor":null}],"herbWarnings":[]},{"id":"mahayogaraj_guggulu","name":"Mahayogaraj guggulu","nameHi":"महायोगराज गुग्गुलु","sanskrit":"Mahayogaraja guggulu","latin":null,"otherNames":["ingredients: Yogaraj guggulu herbs plus guggulu","vanga bhasma (tin)","rajata bhasma (silver)","naga bhasma (lead)","loha bhasma (iron)","abhraka bhasma (mica)","mandura bhasma (iron oxide)","rasa sindoor (mercuric sulphide)"],"kind":"mineral_preparation","dataQuality":"limited","traditionalContext":"A guggul and metal-bhasma tablet traditionally used in Ayurveda for general wellbeing of the joints and musculoskeletal system.","isAyurvedic":true,"commonProducts":["Baidyanath Mahayogaraj guggulu","Dabur Mahayograj guggulu","Sri Sri Ayurveda Mahayogaraj guggulu"],"safetyFlags":[{"flag":"heavy_metals","note":"Contains lead (naga bhasma) and mercury (rasa sindoor) by design. A Mahayogaraj guggulu sample linked to lead poisoning contained 4.9% lead (CDC, 2015); a CCRAS study found 25.8 µg/g lead, above the WHO limit.","evidence":"regulatory","sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15598918/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/18728265/","https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/preview/mmwrhtml/mm5326a3.htm","https://www.fda.gov/drugs/fraudulent-products/fda-warns-about-heavy-metal-poisoning-associated-certain-unapproved-ayurvedic-drug-products","https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/preview/mmwrhtml/mm6432a6.htm","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/21170206/"]},{"flag":"pregnancy","note":"Avoid in pregnancy and breastfeeding unless a doctor advises otherwise: lead poisoning, including miscarriage, was reported in pregnant women using rasa shastra (metal-containing) Ayurvedic medicines.","evidence":"case_reports","sources":["https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/preview/mmwrhtml/mm6133a1.htm"]},{"flag":"children","note":"Keep away from children; severe lead and mercury poisoning has been reported in children given Ayurvedic herbo-mineral remedies.","evidence":"case_reports","sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41052789/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41244251/"]},{"flag":"kidney","note":"Lead and mercury can damage the kidneys; avoid with kidney disease unless a doctor advises otherwise.","evidence":"regulatory","sources":["https://www.fda.gov/drugs/fraudulent-products/fda-warns-about-heavy-metal-poisoning-associated-certain-unapproved-ayurvedic-drug-products","https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/preview/mmwrhtml/mm6432a6.htm"]}],"interactions":[{"drugClass":"cyp3a4_substrate_narrow","severity":"moderate","effect":"may raise levels of medicines broken down by CYP3A4 (e.g. midazolam, tacrolimus, some statins)","mechanism":"product studied: Mahayogaraj guggulu and guggulsterones inhibited CYP3A4 and increased midazolam exposure in rats","evidence":"preclinical","advice":"Talk to your doctor or pharmacist before combining.","sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/33436877/"],"onlyMolecules":null,"majorOnlyFor":null},{"drugClass":"antihypertensive","severity":"moderate","effect":"may lower the effect of propranolol and diltiazem","mechanism":"via ingredient guggulu (Commiphora wightii): single-dose study in healthy volunteers showed reduced Cmax and AUC of propranolol and diltiazem","evidence":"clinical","advice":"Talk to your doctor or pharmacist before combining; your blood pressure or heart rate may need checking.","sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/7852226/"],"onlyMolecules":null,"majorOnlyFor":null},{"drugClass":"nephrotoxic","severity":"moderate","effect":"may add to kidney strain with kidney-toxic medicines","mechanism":"via ingredients naga bhasma (lead) and rasa sindoor (mercury): heavy-metal kidney toxicity (theoretical additive effect)","evidence":"theoretical","advice":"Talk to your doctor or pharmacist before combining.","sources":["https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/preview/mmwrhtml/mm6432a6.htm","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/22441626/"],"onlyMolecules":null,"majorOnlyFor":null}],"herbWarnings":[]},{"id":"chandraprabha_vati","name":"Chandraprabha vati","nameHi":"चन्द्रप्रभा वटी","sanskrit":"Chandraprabha vati","latin":null,"otherNames":["ingredients: shilajit (asphaltum)","guggulu","lauha bhasma (iron)","makshika bhasma (copper-iron pyrite)","sugar","karpura","vacha (Acorus calamus)","musta","guduchi","triphala","trikatu","salts and kshara (alkalis)"],"kind":"mineral_preparation","dataQuality":"limited","traditionalContext":"A herbo-mineral tablet traditionally used in Ayurveda for general wellbeing of the urinary and reproductive systems.","isAyurvedic":true,"commonProducts":["Baidyanath Chandraprabha vati","Dabur Chandraprabha vati","Patanjali Divya Chandraprabha vati"],"safetyFlags":[{"flag":"heavy_metals","note":"Contains mineral bhasmas (iron, copper pyrite) and shilajit; heavy metals were detected in about 40% of rasa shastra products in a 2008 study. Choose tested products.","evidence":"regulatory","sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15598918/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/18728265/","https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/preview/mmwrhtml/mm5326a3.htm","https://www.fda.gov/drugs/fraudulent-products/fda-warns-about-heavy-metal-poisoning-associated-certain-unapproved-ayurvedic-drug-products","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38821011/"]},{"flag":"other","note":"Contains vacha (Acorus calamus); calamus is prohibited from use in human food in the US because of beta-asarone.","evidence":"regulatory","sources":["https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-21/chapter-I/subchapter-B/part-189/subpart-C/section-189.110"]}],"interactions":[{"drugClass":"antihypertensive","severity":"moderate","effect":"may lower the effect of propranolol and diltiazem","mechanism":"via ingredient guggulu (Commiphora wightii): single-dose study in healthy volunteers showed reduced Cmax and AUC of propranolol and diltiazem","evidence":"clinical","advice":"Talk to your doctor or pharmacist before combining; your blood pressure or heart rate may need checking.","sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/7852226/"],"onlyMolecules":null,"majorOnlyFor":null},{"drugClass":"cyp3a4_substrate_narrow","severity":"moderate","effect":"may change levels of medicines broken down by CYP3A4","mechanism":"via ingredient guggulu (Commiphora wightii): guggulsterone activates PXR and induces CYP3A in hepatocytes (lab studies)","evidence":"preclinical","advice":"Talk to your doctor or pharmacist before combining.","sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15075359/","https://www.mskcc.org/cancer-care/integrative-medicine/herbs/guggul"],"onlyMolecules":null,"majorOnlyFor":null},{"drugClass":"thyroid_hormone","severity":"minor","effect":"may reduce absorption of levothyroxine","mechanism":"via ingredient lauha bhasma (iron oxide): iron binds levothyroxine in the gut","evidence":"theoretical","advice":"Talk to your doctor or pharmacist before combining; they may advise spacing doses (often at least 4 hours from levothyroxine).","sources":["https://ods.od.nih.gov/factsheets/Iron-HealthProfessional/"],"onlyMolecules":null,"majorOnlyFor":null},{"drugClass":"antibiotic_chelating","severity":"minor","effect":"may reduce absorption of fluoroquinolone and tetracycline antibiotics","mechanism":"via ingredient lauha bhasma (iron oxide): polyvalent cations chelate these antibiotics","evidence":"theoretical","advice":"Talk to your doctor or pharmacist; antibiotic and mineral doses usually need to be taken hours apart.","sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34866992/"],"onlyMolecules":null,"majorOnlyFor":null},{"drugClass":"antiparkinson_levodopa","severity":"minor","effect":"may reduce absorption and effect of levodopa","mechanism":"via ingredient lauha bhasma (iron oxide): iron may chelate levodopa in the gut; levodopa labels warn about iron-containing supplements","evidence":"theoretical","advice":"Talk to your doctor or pharmacist before combining; doses may need to be spaced apart.","sources":["https://ods.od.nih.gov/factsheets/Iron-HealthProfessional/"],"onlyMolecules":null,"majorOnlyFor":null},{"drugClass":"antidiabetic_insulin","severity":"minor","effect":"may add to the blood-sugar-lowering effect of diabetes medicines and raise the risk of low blood sugar","mechanism":"via ingredients shilajit and guggulu; product unstudied (theoretical)","evidence":"theoretical","advice":"Talk to your doctor or pharmacist before combining; check your blood sugar more often and know the signs of low blood sugar.","sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/23733436/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38821011/"],"onlyMolecules":null,"majorOnlyFor":null},{"drugClass":"antidiabetic_sulfonylurea","severity":"minor","effect":"may add to the blood-sugar-lowering effect of diabetes medicines and raise the risk of low blood sugar","mechanism":"via ingredients shilajit and guggulu; product unstudied (theoretical)","evidence":"theoretical","advice":"Talk to your doctor or pharmacist before combining; check your blood sugar more often and know the signs of low blood sugar.","sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/23733436/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38821011/"],"onlyMolecules":null,"majorOnlyFor":null},{"drugClass":"antidiabetic_other","severity":"minor","effect":"may add to the blood-sugar-lowering effect of diabetes medicines and raise the risk of low blood sugar, especially with other glucose-lowering medicines","mechanism":"via ingredients shilajit and guggulu; product unstudied (theoretical)","evidence":"theoretical","advice":"Talk to your doctor or pharmacist before combining; check your blood sugar more often and know the signs of low blood sugar.","sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/23733436/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38821011/"],"onlyMolecules":null,"majorOnlyFor":null}],"herbWarnings":[]},{"id":"arogyavardhini_vati","name":"Arogyavardhini vati","nameHi":"आरोग्यवर्धिनी वटी","sanskrit":"Arogyavardhini rasa / vati","latin":null,"otherNames":["ingredients: kajjali (purified mercury + sulphur; mercuric sulphide)","tamra bhasma (copper)","lauha bhasma (iron)","abhraka bhasma (mica)","shilajit","guggulu","triphala","chitrak","kutki (Picrorhiza kurroa, largest herbal share)","neem leaf juice"],"kind":"mineral_preparation","dataQuality":"limited","traditionalContext":"A herbo-mineral tablet traditionally used in Ayurveda for general wellbeing of the liver and digestive system.","isAyurvedic":true,"commonProducts":["Baidyanath Arogyavardhini bati","Dabur Arogyavardhini bati","Patanjali Divya Arogyavardhini vati"],"safetyFlags":[{"flag":"heavy_metals","note":"Contains mercury (about 1.5-2.8% in analyses) and copper by design. In rats, Aarogyavardhini Vati led to mercury accumulation in the kidney.","evidence":"regulatory","sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15598918/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/18728265/","https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/preview/mmwrhtml/mm5326a3.htm","https://www.fda.gov/drugs/fraudulent-products/fda-warns-about-heavy-metal-poisoning-associated-certain-unapproved-ayurvedic-drug-products","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32035767/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/22441626/"]},{"flag":"pregnancy","note":"Avoid in pregnancy and breastfeeding unless a doctor advises otherwise: lead poisoning, including miscarriage, was reported in pregnant women using rasa shastra (metal-containing) Ayurvedic medicines.","evidence":"case_reports","sources":["https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/preview/mmwrhtml/mm6133a1.htm"]},{"flag":"children","note":"Keep away from children; severe lead and mercury poisoning has been reported in children given Ayurvedic herbo-mineral remedies.","evidence":"case_reports","sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41052789/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41244251/"]},{"flag":"kidney","note":"Mercury from this product accumulated in rat kidneys; avoid with kidney disease unless a doctor advises otherwise.","evidence":"preclinical","sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32035767/"]}],"interactions":[{"drugClass":"nephrotoxic","severity":"moderate","effect":"may add to kidney strain with kidney-toxic medicines","mechanism":"product studied: mercury accumulated in kidneys of treated rats; additive effect with nephrotoxic drugs is theoretical","evidence":"preclinical","advice":"Talk to your doctor or pharmacist before combining.","sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32035767/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/22441626/"],"onlyMolecules":null,"majorOnlyFor":null},{"drugClass":"antihypertensive","severity":"moderate","effect":"may lower the effect of propranolol and diltiazem","mechanism":"via ingredient guggulu (Commiphora wightii): single-dose study in healthy volunteers showed reduced Cmax and AUC of propranolol and diltiazem","evidence":"clinical","advice":"Talk to your doctor or pharmacist before combining; your blood pressure or heart rate may need checking.","sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/7852226/"],"onlyMolecules":null,"majorOnlyFor":null},{"drugClass":"thyroid_hormone","severity":"minor","effect":"may reduce absorption of levothyroxine","mechanism":"via ingredient lauha bhasma (iron oxide): iron binds levothyroxine in the gut","evidence":"theoretical","advice":"Talk to your doctor or pharmacist before combining; they may advise spacing doses (often at least 4 hours from levothyroxine).","sources":["https://ods.od.nih.gov/factsheets/Iron-HealthProfessional/"],"onlyMolecules":null,"majorOnlyFor":null},{"drugClass":"antibiotic_chelating","severity":"minor","effect":"may reduce absorption of fluoroquinolone and tetracycline antibiotics","mechanism":"via ingredient lauha bhasma (iron oxide): polyvalent cations chelate these antibiotics","evidence":"theoretical","advice":"Talk to your doctor or pharmacist; antibiotic and mineral doses usually need to be taken hours apart.","sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34866992/"],"onlyMolecules":null,"majorOnlyFor":null},{"drugClass":"antiparkinson_levodopa","severity":"minor","effect":"may reduce absorption and effect of levodopa","mechanism":"via ingredient lauha bhasma (iron oxide): iron may chelate levodopa in the gut; levodopa labels warn about iron-containing supplements","evidence":"theoretical","advice":"Talk to your doctor or pharmacist before combining; doses may need to be spaced apart.","sources":["https://ods.od.nih.gov/factsheets/Iron-HealthProfessional/"],"onlyMolecules":null,"majorOnlyFor":null}],"herbWarnings":[]},{"id":"punarnavadi_mandur","name":"Punarnavadi mandur","nameHi":"पुनर्नवादि मण्डूर","sanskrit":"Punarnavadi mandura","latin":null,"otherNames":["ingredients: mandura bhasma (iron oxide; about 40 parts)","punarnava (Boerhavia diffusa)","trivrit","trikatu","triphala","vidanga","devdaru","chitrak","kushtha","haridra","daruharidra","danti","kutki","musta","processed in cow's urine (gomutra)"],"kind":"mineral_preparation","dataQuality":"limited","traditionalContext":"An iron-based herbo-mineral tablet traditionally used in Ayurveda for general wellbeing of the blood.","isAyurvedic":true,"commonProducts":["Baidyanath Punarnavadi mandur","Dabur Punarnavadi mandoor","Patanjali Divya Punarnavadi mandur"],"safetyFlags":[{"flag":"children","note":"Iron-containing products are a classic cause of fatal accidental poisoning in toddlers; store out of reach of children.","evidence":"case_reports","sources":["https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/preview/mmwrhtml/00019593.htm"]},{"flag":"heavy_metals","note":"Herbo-mineral (rasa shastra) product; heavy metals have been found in a share of such products. Choose tested products.","evidence":"regulatory","sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15598918/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/18728265/","https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/preview/mmwrhtml/mm5326a3.htm","https://www.fda.gov/drugs/fraudulent-products/fda-warns-about-heavy-metal-poisoning-associated-certain-unapproved-ayurvedic-drug-products","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/37153070/"]}],"interactions":[{"drugClass":"thyroid_hormone","severity":"moderate","effect":"may reduce absorption of levothyroxine","mechanism":"via ingredient mandura bhasma (iron oxide): iron binds levothyroxine in the gut","evidence":"clinical","advice":"Talk to your doctor or pharmacist before combining; they may advise spacing doses (often at least 4 hours from levothyroxine).","sources":["https://ods.od.nih.gov/factsheets/Iron-HealthProfessional/"],"onlyMolecules":null,"majorOnlyFor":null},{"drugClass":"antibiotic_chelating","severity":"moderate","effect":"may reduce absorption of fluoroquinolone and tetracycline antibiotics","mechanism":"via ingredient mandura bhasma (iron oxide): polyvalent cations chelate these antibiotics","evidence":"clinical","advice":"Talk to your doctor or pharmacist; antibiotic and mineral doses usually need to be taken hours apart.","sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34866992/"],"onlyMolecules":null,"majorOnlyFor":null},{"drugClass":"antiparkinson_levodopa","severity":"moderate","effect":"may reduce absorption and effect of levodopa","mechanism":"via ingredient mandura bhasma (iron oxide): iron may chelate levodopa in the gut; levodopa labels warn about iron-containing supplements","evidence":"clinical","advice":"Talk to your doctor or pharmacist before combining; doses may need to be spaced apart.","sources":["https://ods.od.nih.gov/factsheets/Iron-HealthProfessional/"],"onlyMolecules":null,"majorOnlyFor":null},{"drugClass":"ppi_antacid","severity":"minor","effect":"acid-reducing medicines may reduce iron absorption from the product","mechanism":"via ingredient mandura bhasma (iron oxide): gastric acid is needed for non-heme iron absorption","evidence":"clinical","advice":"Talk to your doctor or pharmacist before combining.","sources":["https://ods.od.nih.gov/factsheets/Iron-HealthProfessional/"],"onlyMolecules":null,"majorOnlyFor":null}],"herbWarnings":[]},{"id":"swarna_bhasma","name":"Swarna bhasma (gold calx)","nameHi":"स्वर्ण भस्म","sanskrit":"Suvarna / Swarna bhasma","latin":null,"otherNames":["ingredients: processed gold (gold micro- and nano-particles)","found in 'swarna yukt' formulations, e.g. Swarna vasant malti, Brihat vata chintamani ras, Garbha chintamani ras (swarna yukt)"],"kind":"mineral_preparation","dataQuality":"poor","traditionalContext":"A processed gold preparation traditionally used in Ayurveda as a rasayana for general wellbeing.","isAyurvedic":true,"commonProducts":["Baidyanath Swarna bhasma","Dabur Swarna bhasma","Swarna yukt (gold-containing) ras/vati products"],"safetyFlags":[{"flag":"heavy_metals","note":"Gold bhasma itself showed little toxicity in rat studies, but gold-containing ('swarna yukt') multi-mineral products have been implicated in lead poisoning (e.g. a 'Swarna Yukt' product in the CDC NYC 2011-2012 cases); many contain mercury or lead too.","evidence":"regulatory","sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15598918/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/18728265/","https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/preview/mmwrhtml/mm5326a3.htm","https://www.fda.gov/drugs/fraudulent-products/fda-warns-about-heavy-metal-poisoning-associated-certain-unapproved-ayurvedic-drug-products","https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/preview/mmwrhtml/mm6133a1.htm","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31730889/"]},{"flag":"pregnancy","note":"Avoid in pregnancy and breastfeeding unless a doctor advises otherwise: lead poisoning, including miscarriage, was reported in pregnant women using rasa shastra (metal-containing) Ayurvedic medicines.","evidence":"case_reports","sources":["https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/preview/mmwrhtml/mm6133a1.htm"]},{"flag":"children","note":"Keep away from children; severe lead and mercury poisoning has been reported in children given Ayurvedic herbo-mineral remedies.","evidence":"case_reports","sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41052789/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41244251/"]}],"interactions":[],"herbWarnings":[]},{"id":"lauha_bhasma","name":"Lauha bhasma (iron calx)","nameHi":"लौह भस्म","sanskrit":"Lauha / Loha bhasma","latin":null,"otherNames":["ingredients: processed iron (iron oxides, mainly Fe2O3/Fe3O4)","also in Chandraprabha vati, Arogyavardhini vati, Navayas lauh, Kumaryasava (some recipes)"],"kind":"mineral_preparation","dataQuality":"limited","traditionalContext":"A processed iron preparation traditionally used in Ayurveda for general wellbeing of the blood.","isAyurvedic":true,"commonProducts":["Baidyanath Lauh bhasma","Dabur Lauh bhasma","Navayas lauh","Saptamrit lauh"],"safetyFlags":[{"flag":"children","note":"Iron-containing products are a classic cause of fatal accidental poisoning in toddlers; store out of reach of children.","evidence":"case_reports","sources":["https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/preview/mmwrhtml/00019593.htm"]},{"flag":"heavy_metals","note":"Characterisation studies show iron oxides with trace contaminants; heavy metals have been found in a share of rasa shastra products. Choose tested products.","evidence":"regulatory","sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15598918/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/18728265/","https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/preview/mmwrhtml/mm5326a3.htm","https://www.fda.gov/drugs/fraudulent-products/fda-warns-about-heavy-metal-poisoning-associated-certain-unapproved-ayurvedic-drug-products","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/23049200/"]}],"interactions":[{"drugClass":"thyroid_hormone","seve